+
+## Future harness batching revision (native pilot required)
+
+The original orchestration bytes are retained as `rule10_prepare-v1.py`,
+`rule10_controls-v1.py` and `RULE10-README-v1.md`. Existing `final1` sources,
+request records and active native checks are unchanged. New editions use the
+shared `rule10_prepare.CHUNK_SIZE = 2048` and shared `seal_chunks` metadata.
+The current closures have fewer than 1600 requests, so each new install/EOF
+phase uses one runtime String-encoded batch instead of twelve 128-row batches.
+This removes repeated full-environment catalogue scans and repeated complete
+instance-lookup snapshot pairs; it removes no requested name or per-row check.
+
+For newly generated install commands only, per-name command elaboration is
+replaced by:
+
+```lean
+Lean.Elab.Command.liftCoreM <|
+  Lean.Attribute.add n `irreducible Lean.Syntax.missing .local
+```
+
+At the pinned Lean 4.25.0 source, `AttrM` is `CoreM`, `Attribute.add` retrieves
+the registered attribute implementation and calls its `add` handler, and
+`irreducible` registers `addAttr .irreducible`. That handler accepts the simple
+attribute's missing syntax, runs the ordinary reducibility safety validation,
+and applies the requested **local** attribute in the current namespace.
+The harness never calls the direct status setter and never enables unsafe
+reducibility. Exact Name/display ambiguity, home, definition kind, components,
+matcher/abbreviation/instance metadata, installed status, full unfolding-mask
+installation/EOF checks and unchanged typeclass lookup comparisons remain.
+
+This is a source-reviewed performance change, not a native success assertion.
+The root must use a fresh edition, pilot the paired controls and a complete
+whole-file seal serially, and verify every raw mask/component/count record
+before relying on the new harness. Preserve the original `final1` run and all
+new pilot attempts in the evidence payload.
